.TH CHANGELOG-CONFIG 5 "July 2026" "changelog 1.0.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
changelog config \- changelog.yaml configuration file format and options reference
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The changelog.yaml configuration file controls how fragments are processed, sorted, and rendered into release notes. It defines project metadata, section customization, output formatting, and plugin documentation settings.

This file is created by \fBchangelog init\fR with sensible defaults that can be customized for specific project needs. See \fBchangelog-init(8)\fR for initialization details.
.SH FILE LOCATION
.PP
By default, configuration is stored at:
.IP \(bu 2
\fIchangelogs/config.yaml\fR in the project root

.TP
.B Alternative Locations:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Custom paths via \fB\-\-dir\fR flag on individual commands
.IP \(bu 2
Legacy locations: \fI.changelogs/config.yaml\fR or \fI.changelog/config.yaml\fR (auto-detected)
.RE

.SH CONFIGURATION OPTIONS
.PP
All configuration fields with their defaults and descriptions:

.TP
.B Required Fields:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtitle:\fR Project title displayed in changelog headers. Example: "MyAwesomeProject"
.RE

.TP
.B Versioning Configuration:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBversion_pattern:\fR Regex pattern for validating version strings (default: "^\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+$")
.IP \(bu 2
\fBus_semantic_versioning:\fR Enforce semantic versioning rules (default: false)
.RE

.TP
.B Fragment Processing:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBkeep_fragments:\fR Retain fragments after release processing (default: false, archives them)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBignore_other_fragment_extensions:\fR Only process .md/.yml files, ignore others (default: true)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsanitize_changelog:\fR Run body through markdown formatter for consistency (default: true)
.RE

.TP
.B Section Customization:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsections:\fR Map of internal category keys to display titles. Example: {"bugfixes": "Bug Fixes"}
.IP \(bu 2
\fBprelude_section_title:\fR Title for unreleased/pre-release section (default: "## [Unreleased]")
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtrivial_section_name:\fR Name for trivial/unchanged section header (default: "Trivial")
.RE

.TP
.B Output Formatting:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBoutput_formats:\fR List of output formats to generate (default: ["markdown"])
.IP \(bu 2
\fBchanges_format:\fR How to render fragment bodies ("raw", "markdown", etc.)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBchangelog_sort:\fR Field to sort entries by ("none", "issue", "date") (default: "none")
.RE

.TP
.B Plugin Documentation (for Ansible collections):
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBusFQCN:\fR Use fully qualified collection names in output (default: false)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBadd_plugin_period:\fR Add period after plugin names in documentation (default: false)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBflatmap:\fR Use short plugin names instead of FQCN (nil=unset, true=enabled, false=disabled)
.RE

.TP
.B Archive and Metadata:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBarchive_path_template:\fR Destination directory for archived fragments (default: ".changelogs/archive")
.IP \(bu 2
\fBchanges_file:\fR Machine-readable metadata file path (default: ".changes.yaml")
.IP \(bu 2
\fBrelease_tag_re:\fR Regex matching stable release tags (default: "((?:[\\d.ab]|rc)+)")
.RE

.SH EXAMPLE CONFIGURATION
.PP
Complete example with common customizations:

.nf
    title: "My Awesome Project"
    version_pattern: "^v\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+$"
    keep_fragments: false
    sanitize_changelog: true

    sections:
      bugfixes: "Bug Fixes & Improvements"
      major_changes: "Major New Features"
      minor_changes: "Minor Enhancements"
      breaking_changes: "Breaking Changes / Migration Guide"

    output_formats:
      - markdown

    changes_format: raw
    changelog_sort: issue

    archive_path_template: ".changelogs/archive/{{version}}"
    changes_file: ".changes.yaml"
.fi

.TP
.B Collection-Specific Configuration:
.nf
    title: "My Ansible Collection"
    is_collection: true
    use_fqcn: true
    add_plugin_period: true

    sections:
      bugfixes: "Bug Fixes"
      minor_changes: "Plugin Enhancements"
      breaking_changes: "Breaking Changes / Plugin Migration Guide"
.fi

.SH SECTION PRIORITY AND SORTING
.PP
Fragments are rendered in this priority order (highest first):

.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
1. Breaking Changes / Porting Guide
.IP \(bu 2
2. Major Changes
.IP \(bu 2
3. Deprecated Features
.IP \(bu 2
4. Removed Features
.IP \(bu 2
5. Bugfixes
.IP \(bu 2
6. Security Fixes
.IP \(bu 2
7. Minor Changes
.IP \(bu 2
8. Known Issues
.RE

.TP
.B Custom Sorting:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBchangelog_sort: issue\fR \- Sort by issue ID numerically/alphabetically
.IP \(bu 2
\fBchangelog_sort: date\fR \- Sort by fragment date field chronologically
.IP \(bu 2
\fBchangelog_sort: none\fR (default) \- Maintain natural file order in directory
.RE

.SH NOTES DIRECTORIES
.PP
Additional fragment directories can be configured for organizing changes by subsystem or team:

.TP
.B Configuration:
.nf
    notes_dirs:
      - changelogs/fragments/core
      - changelogs/notes/community
      - plugins/legacy_changes
.fi

.TP
.B Behavior:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Later directories override earlier ones for same-named fragments
.IP \(bu 2
All notes directories are merged during release/generate operations
.IP \(bu 2
Can be specified dynamically via \fB\-\-notes-dir\fR command flags
.RE

.SH SEE ALSO
.TP
\fBchangelog(8)\fR \- Main changelog command with configuration overview
.TP
\fBchangelog-init(8)\fR \- Initialize project with default configuration
.TP
\fBchangelog-reformat(8)\fR \- Reformat and normalize configuration files
